{
  "task": "MA-8 / messaging-attention sections 3 and 7",
  "summary": [
    "Operator CLI and Settings change another seat policy through the same generation-fenced, journaled operator path; a seat MCP caller retains its own authority.",
    "Setter grammar: ctl seat attention <seat> <direct|destination> <conversation|event> <wake|inbox|digest|default>; the existing read grammar remains.",
    "A default choice removes exactly its destination/class override, preserves unrelated rules and stores None when no overrides remain.",
    "Retries keep their operation id; different arguments with that id are refused by the existing operator journal.",
    "Settings reads one selected policy, caches one immutable seat view, and refreshes once when its seat/generation/role changes; no frame polling.",
    "Channel names use a bounded BTreeMap prefix range, not an all-seat tree traversal or a copy on every ordinary row.",
    "Ordinary observations carry only pending digest count/deadline or a labelled observation error; indexed counts use active members, not historical window totals.",
    "Receipt changes travel through the existing GUI events lane; no new socket, consumer, delivery scheduler or tracing is introduced.",
    "The real private-account headless test proves CLI set/reset/replay/refusal plus a Settings key edit, with an actually produced frame; no operator identity or window.",
    "All 200 moved/new Settings cases and eight digest-row cases pass: 208 measured, zero unproven, zero geometry mismatch, zero pixel reviews.",
    "The first five-case comparison exposed card/header spacing, title weight and mute-margin errors; corrected to the measured lab reference, then five and 208 cases passed.",
    "The first native test expected an unpromised op_id_reused spelling; it now asserts the existing refusal. Its next run found the missing live Settings whitelist; that product path is fixed.",
    "Strict Clippy findings were fixed by boxing the Settings controller and using a direct record initializer; no lint suppression or threshold change.",
    "Role defaults(), own-seat MCP policy semantics and pinned delivery decisions remain with the existing owners; Velvet owns the separate 817e4b43 defaults correction.",
    "No 967-seat timing, native notification presentation or photon/scanout claim. Author presubmit and postsubmit acceptance are separate."
  ],
  "mechanisms": {
    "crates/bbt-mux/src/registry.rs:79": "atomic scoped reset and generation fence",
    "crates/bbt-mux/src/logic.rs:4764": "operator journal and state publication for a policy edit",
    "crates/bbt-mux/src/messaging/ledger.rs:621": "recipient-indexed active digest member count and next eligibility",
    "crates/bbt-mux/src/messaging/tree.rs:174": "bounded channel-prefix read excludes seat subtrees",
    "crates/bbt-mux/src/gui_events.rs:27": "existing receipt lane refreshes affected seat observations",
    "crates/bboxy450-term/src/main.rs:2104": "one contextual nonblocking read per selected seat/generation/role",
    "crates/bboxy450-term/src/settings/messaging.rs:38": "confirmed policy, mute, defaults and pending-count projection",
    "crates/bbt-ui/src/modules/settings/messaging.rs:68": "native Messaging section and live operator intents"
  },
